/*! @brief XmlDocument is an object of the xml module, representing the entire XML document, providing access to the entire document

XmlDocument is the root of a document tree, containing all nodes in the entire XML document. The XmlDocument object also provides the following functions:

1. Create element nodes, text nodes, comments, and processing instructions, etc.
2. Access and modify document properties and related information (such as DTD comments and document declarations)
3. Parse XML documents

Below is example code for using the XmlDocument object to parse an XML document:

```JavaScript
var xml = require('xml');
var fs = require('fs');

var xmlStr = fs.readFile('test.xml');
var xmlDoc = xml.parse(xmlStr);

// get document root node name
var rootName = xmlDoc.documentElement.nodeName;
console.log(`The document root node name is ${rootName}`);
```

In the above code, we first use the `readFile()` method of the `fs` module to read an XML file, and assign the file stream to the variable `xmlStr`. Then we use the `parse()` method of the `xml` module to parse the XML file, and assign the parsed `XmlDocument` object to the variable `xmlDoc`. Finally, we use the `documentElement` property of `xmlDoc` to get the document root node, get its node name, and output it to the console.

Since XmlDocument is the entry point for the entire XML document, we can get and modify related information of the document through it. For example, we can get and modify the XML version and standalone attributes of the document through `xmlDoc.xmlVersion` and `xmlDoc.xmlStandalone` respectively. We can also create new processing instruction nodes through the `xmlDoc.createProcessingInstruction()` method.

The XmlDocument object is a very powerful type, providing great convenience for us to handle parsing XML files.
*/
interface XmlDocument : XmlNode
{
    /*! @brief Construct an XmlDocument object
     @param type Specify the type of the document object, default is "text/xml", if you need to process html, specify "text/html"
    */
    XmlDocument(String type = "text/xml");

    /*! @brief Compose the document by parsing an XML/HTML string, does not support multiple languages
     @param source The XML/HTML text to be parsed, depending on the type when the document was created
    */
    load(String source);

    /*! @brief Compose the document by parsing a binary XML/HTML string, and automatically convert according to the language
     @param source The XML/HTML text to be parsed, depending on the type when the document was created
    */
    load(Buffer source);

    /*! @brief Return the encoding used for the document (when parsing)
    */
    readonly String inputEncoding;

    /*! @brief Set or return whether the document is standalone
    */
    Boolean xmlStandalone;

    /*! @brief Set or return the XML version of the document
    */
    String xmlVersion;

    /*! @brief Return the document type declaration (Document Type Declaration) associated with the document

    For XML documents without DTD, return null. This property provides direct access to the XmlDocumentType object (a child node of XmlDocument).
    */
    readonly XmlDocumentType doctype;

    /*! @brief Return the root node of the document
    */
    readonly XmlElement documentElement;

    /*! @brief Return the head node of the HTML document, only valid in html mode
    */
    readonly XmlElement head;

    /*! @brief Return the content of the title node of the HTML document, only valid in html mode
    */
    readonly String title;

    /*! @brief Return the body node of the HTML document, only valid in html mode
    */
    readonly XmlElement body;

    /*! @brief Return a node list of all elements with the specified name

     This method will return an XmlNodeList object (which can be treated as a read-only array), which stores all XmlElement nodes in the document with the specified tag name, in the order they appear in the source document. The XmlNodeList object is "live", meaning that if elements with the specified tag name are added or removed in the document, its content will be automatically updated as necessary.
     @param tagName The tag name to be retrieved. The value "*" matches all tags
     @return An XmlNodeList collection of XmlElement nodes with the specified tag in the document tree. The order of the returned element nodes is the order they appear in the source document.
    */
    XmlNodeList getElementsByTagName(String tagName);

    /*! @brief Return a node list of all elements with the specified namespace and name

     This method is similar to getElementsByTagName(), but it retrieves elements based on namespace and name.
     @param namespaceURI Specify the namespace URI to be retrieved. The value "*" can match all tags
     @param localName The tag name to be retrieved. The value "*" matches all tags
     @return An XmlNodeList collection of XmlElement nodes with the specified tag in the document tree. The order of the returned element nodes is the order they appear in the source document.
    */
    XmlNodeList getElementsByTagNameNS(String namespaceURI, String localName);

    /*! @brief Return the element with the specified id attribute

     This method will traverse the descendant nodes of the document, returning an XmlElement node object, representing the first document element with the specified id attribute.
     @param id The id to be retrieved
     @return The XmlElement node with the specified id attribute in the node tree
    */
    XmlElement getElementById(String id);

    /*! @brief Return a node list of all elements with the specified class name

     This method will return an XmlNodeList object (which can be treated as a read-only array), which stores all XmlElement nodes in the document with the specified class name, in the order they appear in the source document. The XmlNodeList object is "live", meaning that if elements with the specified tag name are added or removed in the document, its content will be automatically updated as necessary.
     @param className The class name to be retrieved
     @return An XmlNodeList collection of XmlElement nodes with the specified class name in the document tree. The order of the returned element nodes is the order they appear in the source document.
    */
    XmlNodeList getElementsByClassName(String className);

    /*! @brief Create an element node
     @param tagName Specify the prescribed name of the element node
     @return Return the newly created XmlElement node with the specified tag name
    */
    XmlElement createElement(String tagName);

    /*! @brief Create an element node with the specified namespace
     @param namespaceURI Specify the namespace URI of the element node
     @param qualifiedName Specify the prescribed name of the element node
     @return Return the newly created XmlElement node with the specified tag name
    */
    XmlElement createElementNS(String namespaceURI, String qualifiedName);

    /*! @brief Create a text node
     @param data Specify the text of this node
     @return Return the newly created XmlText node representing the specified data string
    */
    XmlText createTextNode(String data);

    /*! @brief Create a comment node
     @param data Specify the comment text of this node
     @return Return the newly created XmlComment node with comment text as the specified data
    */
    XmlComment createComment(String data);

    /*! @brief Create an XmlCDATASection node
     @param data Specify the CDATA data prescribed for this node
     @return Return the newly created XmlCDATASection node with content as the specified data
    */
    XmlCDATASection createCDATASection(String data);

    /*! @brief Create an XmlProcessingInstruction node
     @param target Specify the target of the processing instruction
     @param data Specify the content text of the processing instruction
     @return The newly created ProcessingInstruction node
    */
    XmlProcessingInstruction createProcessingInstruction(String target, String data);
    /*! @brief Create an empty XmlDocumentFragment node

     DocumentFragment is a lightweight document object that can contain multiple child nodes. When a DocumentFragment is inserted into a document, it is not the DocumentFragment itself that is inserted, but all of its child nodes.
     @return The newly created XmlDocumentFragment node
    */
    XmlDocumentFragment createDocumentFragment();

    /*! @brief Import a node from another document into this document

     This method creates a copy of the source node that can be inserted into this document. The source node remains unchanged. If you need to move a node from another document to this document instead of copying, use the adoptNode method.
     @param importedNode The node to import
     @param deep If true, recursively import the entire subtree of the node; if false, import only the node itself
     @return The newly imported node belonging to this document
    */
    XmlNode importNode(XmlNode importedNode, Boolean deep = true);

    /*! @brief Adopt a node from another document into this document

     This method moves a node from another document to this document. The node is removed from the original document, and its ownerDocument property is changed to this document. Unlike importNode, adoptNode does not create a copy.
     @param adoptedNode The node to adopt
     @return The adopted node
    */
    XmlNode adoptNode(XmlNode adoptedNode);
    /*! @brief Return an XmlNodeList of elements that match the specified CSS selector

     This method will return an XmlNodeList object (which can be treated as a read-only array), which stores all XmlElement nodes in the document that match the specified CSS selector, in the order they appear in the source document. The XmlNodeList object is "live", meaning that if elements that match the specified selector are added or removed in the document, its content will be automatically updated as necessary.
     @param selectors Specify the CSS selector
     @return XmlElement nodes that match the specified CSS selector
    */
    XmlElement querySelector(String selectors);

    /*! @brief Return an XmlNodeList of all elements that match the specified CSS selector

     This method will return an XmlNodeList object (which can be treated as a read-only array), which stores all XmlElement nodes in the document that match the specified CSS selector, in the order they appear in the source document. The XmlNodeList object is "live", meaning that if elements that match the specified selector are added or removed in the document, its content will be automatically updated as necessary.
     @param selectors Specify the CSS selector
     @return An XmlNodeList collection of XmlElement nodes that match the specified CSS selector. The order of the returned element nodes is the order they appear in the source document.
    */
    XmlNodeList querySelectorAll(String selectors);
};